  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "How you feel, and what you are like",
      "title_cz": "Jak se cítíte a jací jste",
      "diagram": "contrast",
      "labels": [
        "angry",
        "kind",
        "how I feel now",
        "what I am like"
      ],
      "body": "25 words for feelings, and almost all of them are adjectives after am or is: I am bored. He is polite.\nSome say how you feel at this moment (angry, nervous, excited, worried, confused). Others describe the person, not the moment (kind, polite, honest, rude, serious). Same frame, two different jobs.",
      "body_cz": "Skoro všechna tato slova jsou přídavná jména po am / is. Některá popisují náladu, jiná povahu."
    },
    {
      "title": "You will use these words in",
      "frames": [
        "I am …",
        "He is …",
        "I have a …",
        "I have …"
      ],
      "note": "Czech says Mám strach — have. English says I am afraid — be. Here the feeling is an adjective, not a thing you own.",
      "note_cz": "Mám strach → I am afraid, ne *I have fear*."
    }
  ],
